# sync_timedb hot-path janitor lock priority

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

**Law:** ingest/populate/append is the **hot path**; janitor seal/dedupe/delete/tar-drop is the **cold path**. Janitor **defers before write** and **cooperatively yields mid-mutation** when ingest signals need the same daily tar after a janitor-first lock — **except daily tar restore from sealed** (missing or corrupt `.tar`), where restore runs to completion and populate **waits** on `daily_tar_restore`. **Archive append dispatch** must still **skip** restore-blocked calendar days (overflow + short backoff) so free archive-pool slots drain other heap days; restore ownership stays on the decompress/day-close thread.

